           <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="la" resp="#SPS">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><persName type="divine" key="nemesisAugusta"><name>Nemesi</name>
                    <lb n="2"/><name><expan><abbr>Aug</abbr><ex>ustae</ex></expan></name></persName> <expan><abbr>sac</abbr><ex>rum</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="3"/><persName type="attested"><name><expan><abbr>G</abbr><ex>aius</ex></expan></name> <name>Lecan 
                    <lb n="4" break="no"/>ius</name> <name>Vita
                    <lb n="5" break="no"/>lis</name></persName> qui et
                    <lb n="6"/><name>Serpulli
                    <lb n="7" break="no"/>us</name> libe<supplied reason="lost">ns</supplied>
                    <lb n="8"/>posu<supplied reason="lost">it</supplied>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app><note>Text mostly from EDR. I disagree, however, with EDR on line 4, where they have recorded a C, I have recorded a G which is clearly visible on the stone.</note></app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#SPS">
                <p>Sacred to Nemesis Augusta, Gaius Lecanius Vitalis, who is also known as Serpullius, gave [this] freely.</p>
            </div>
